Ritual — web app only (Flutter web + Node backend). No mobile/desktop targets.

──────────────────────────────────────────────

Backend (start Node — always run first):
cd "/Users/radhikamaheshwari/Desktop/Learning 2026/Projects/Ritual/backend"
npm run dev
Runs on http://localhost:5001 (PORT is set in backend/.env)
NOTE: don't use port 5000 on macOS — AirPlay Receiver (Control Center) already
listens there. Fly.io uses 5000 inside the container, which is fine.
Health check: curl http://localhost:5001/health

──────────────────────────────────────────────

Frontend — local dev (hot reload):
cd "/Users/radhikamaheshwari/Desktop/Learning 2026/Projects/Ritual/app"
flutter run -d chrome --dart-define=BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5001

Omit --dart-define to point at the deployed backend
(default: https://ritual-backend.fly.dev — see lib/core/network/api_client.dart)

──────────────────────────────────────────────

Frontend — production build:
cd "/Users/radhikamaheshwari/Desktop/Learning 2026/Projects/Ritual/app"
flutter build web --release --dart-define=BACKEND_URL=https://ritual-backend.fly.dev

Deploy to Firebase Hosting (serves app/build/web, see firebase.json):
cd "/Users/radhikamaheshwari/Desktop/Learning 2026/Projects/Ritual"
firebase deploy --only hosting

Serve the build locally instead:
cd "/Users/radhikamaheshwari/Desktop/Learning 2026/Projects/Ritual/app/build/web"
python3 -m http.server 8080
open http://localhost:8080
